{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-94734e07-1ca7-4695-827c-989d72d73339","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a73b6915999a848","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9001-_zc5cp1_/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9001-E001.md","content":"# Surface InferenceService deployment status in the Dashboard model serving views\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers deployment status visibility for KServe InferenceService\nmodels directly in the RHOAI Dashboard, so data scientists can tell whether a\ndeployment is healthy without leaving the console or using `oc` commands. It\ncovers the status display in the model serving views, a status detail view\nwith underlying condition messages and recent events, automatic status\nfreshness, and filter/sort by status.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Display a deployment status — Ready, Progressing, Failed — for each deployed\n  KServe InferenceService model in the Dashboard model serving views, derived\n  from the InferenceService CR status conditions.\n- Add a status detail view showing the underlying condition messages and\n  recent Kubernetes events for a failed or progressing deployment.\n- Ensure the displayed status reflects the actual InferenceService state\n  within 30 seconds of a change, without a manual page reload. The refresh\n  mechanism (polling interval vs. Kubernetes watch) is an implementation\n  decision for the Dashboard team.\n- Add filter and sort controls for the deployed models list by status.\n- Scope is limited to KServe InferenceService deployments; ModelMesh\n  deployments, alerting/notifications on status transitions, and status\n  history / timeline views are out of scope per the strategy.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Each deployed KServe InferenceService shown in the Dashboard model serving\n  views displays one of the statuses Ready, Progressing, or Failed, derived\n  from the InferenceService status conditions.\n- A user can open a status detail view for a failed or progressing deployment\n  that shows the underlying condition messages and recent events.\n- After a change in the actual InferenceService state, the displayed status\n  reflects the new state within 30 seconds without a manual page reload.\n- The deployed models list can be filtered by status and sorted by status.\n- The condition-to-status mapping used by the Dashboard has been validated\n  with the RHOAI Serving team against actual InferenceService conditions in\n  both serverless and raw deployment modes.\n- The Dashboard build and test pipeline passes with these changes.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): Users see a deployment status for each deployed model in the\n  Dashboard model serving views.\n- HLR-2 (P0): Users can open a status detail view showing the underlying\n  condition messages and recent events for a failed or progressing deployment.\n- HLR-3 (P1): Displayed status reflects the actual InferenceService state\n  within 30 seconds of a change, without a manual page reload.\n- HLR-4 (P2): Users can filter and sort the deployed models list by status.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":30140,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aaf76ca7e81e0ca3","agent_id":"a595dbf416503af2e","session_id":"d9a0c1a1-801a-4eeb-bfda-a0400f18f850","uuid":"56c0db3e-6d5c-4bf7-ba4f-882968c3ee01","timestamp":"2026-10-22T17:30:40.106Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9001"}
