{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9bc0832729bc0088","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9001-E002\n3\ttitle: Validate KServe InferenceService status conditions for Dashboard consumption\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9001\n5\tcomponent: KServe\n6\tteam: RHOAI Serving\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Validate KServe InferenceService status conditions for Dashboard consumption\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic validates that the InferenceService status conditions and\n34\tKubernetes events exposed by KServe are complete, stable, and accessible\n35\tenough for the RHOAI Dashboard to derive and surface deployment status\n36\t(Ready, Progressing, Failed). KServe requires no code changes for this\n37\tstrategy; this is the serving team's validation of the passive component it\n38\towns, producing an agreed condition-to-status mapping contract for the\n39\tDashboard implementation.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Enumerate the InferenceService CR status conditions and related Kubernetes\n44\t  events in both serverless and raw deployment modes.\n45\t- Confirm the conditions are sufficient to derive each of Ready, Progressing,\n46\t  and Failed, including failure paths (for example, a predictor that fails to\n47\t  become ready), and identify any gaps.\n48\t- Confirm the condition messages and recent events needed by a status detail\n49\t  view are accessible with the permissions of typical Dashboard users.\n50\t- Produce an agreed condition-to-status mapping document for Dashboard\n51\t  consumption, covering both deployment modes.\n52\t- No KServe code changes are expected; if gaps are found, document them with\n53\t  a recommended fallback (for example, an alternate condition or event source)\n54\t  rather than fixing KServe in this epic.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- A condition-to-status mapping covering both serverless and raw deployment\n59\t  modes exists and is agreed with the RHOAI Dashboard team.\n60\t- Each of Ready, Progressing, and Failed is derivable from the documented\n61\t  conditions, or any gap is documented together with a fallback the Dashboard\n62\t  can use.\n63\t- Representative failure scenarios (for example, a failed predictor rollout)\n64\t  are verified to produce conditions and events that the mapping classifies\n65\t  as Failed.\n66\t- The accessibility of status conditions and recent events for typical\n67\t  Dashboard user permissions is confirmed and documented.\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- HLR-1 (P0, validation): the deployment status shown by the Dashboard is\n72\t  derived from validated InferenceService status conditions.\n73\t- HLR-2 (P0, validation): the condition messages and recent events shown in\n74\t  the status detail view are validated as present and accessible.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a8de3d9923dfaffe","agent_id":"a8c3ab3d9ba3aab85","session_id":"d9a0c1a1-801a-4eeb-bfda-a0400f18f850","uuid":"b36c2cef-2fa8-4bba-b4cf-3f03293460b0","timestamp":"2026-10-22T17:36:42.586Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9bc0832729bc0088","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9001 decomposition"}
